<TITLE>Error Code Display Function</TITLE>
<LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>The Toll Collection (ETC) Computer Assembly stores the last unified error code that occurred (only 1), and the unified error code can be announced by displaying the registration information on the display with ACC or IG ON, or by pressing the usage history check button of the Toll Collection (ETC) Computer Assembly for 2 seconds or more with no ETC card inserted.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>If there is a malfunction in the Toll Collection (ETC) Computer Assembly or the ETC card, a unified error code such as those in the table (Unified Error Code List) is shown on the display (registration information screen/interrupt display) to notify the user of the malfunction.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<TABLE FRAME = "ALL" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1"><TITLE>Unified Error Code List</TITLE>
<TGROUP COLS = "2" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1" TGROUPSTYLE = "Table_10">
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "1" COLNAME = "1" COLWIDTH = "28%"/>
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "2" COLNAME = "2" COLWIDTH = "71%"/>
<THEAD>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" CONSPIC = "0"><PTXT>Unified Error Code</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" CONSPIC = "0"><PTXT>Abnormal Condition</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
</THEAD>
<TBODY>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE" ALIGN = "CENTER" CONSPIC = "0">
<PTXT>01</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" VALIGN = "MIDDLE" CONSPIC = "0"><PTXT>ETC Card Insertion Error</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
